What the implementation does (summary)\
- Uses MovieLens 100k data (ml-100k) and filters users/items by minimum counts, then remaps IDs to a compact 0-based indexing.\
- Performs a per-user stratified train/test split (80% train, 20% test).\
- Builds a simple item-based collaborative filtering model:\
  - Computes global mean mu_global and per-item means (item_means).\
  - Builds a user-item rating matrix R and a centered version Rc using item means.\
  - Computes item-item similarities S from Rc^T Rc, normalizes, and zeroes the diagonal.\
  - For each test interaction (user u, item i), predicts rating as:\
    pred = mu_i + sum_j (w_i_j * (r_u_j - mu_j)) / sum_j |w_i_j|\
    where w_i_j = S[i, j] and r_u_j are the user\'92s ratings for neighbor items j. If no contributing neighbors exist, predict mu_global.\
  - Tracks coverage (how often a valid prediction could be made using neighbors).\
- Evaluates performance with RMSE and MAE, plus two baselines:\
  - Global baseline: always predicting mu_global.\
  - User baseline: using the user\'92s mean rating when available, else mu_global.\
- Also includes a helper to produce simple Top-5 recommendations for a given user using the learned neighbors and item means.\
- Saves a numpy file experiment_data.npy with the run results.\
